# Decimal subtraction with integer operands

Subtracts 5 from 2.30 in both operand orders to verify the integer is
promoted and the result stays an exact decimal whose sign follows the
operand order, producing -2.70 and 2.70.

>>> source
integer_right: int = 5
decimal_left: decimal = 2.30

// Verifies the Decimal/Int promotion.
decimal_minus_integer: decimal = decimal_left - integer_right
print(decimal_minus_integer)

// Verifies the same promotion with the operand order reversed.
integer_minus_decimal: decimal = integer_right - decimal_left
print(integer_minus_decimal)

<<< stdout
-2.70
2.70

<<< stderr
